Description: web browser for the hibr desktop, on WPE WebKit
 The engine of hibr's Browser app and a module that gives hibr the `web`
 verbs over it: WPE WebKit 2.54.1, built from upstream, running headless in a
 helper process of its own (no GTK, no X, no Wayland), with JavaScript, a
 JIT, WebAssembly and media source playback. Pages are drawn as pixels,
 as cells, or as text.
 .
 It also carries a second, light engine, hibr-lx (Lexbor for HTML, its own
 cascade and layout in terminal cells, QuickJS-ng for scripts), chosen
 per tab (`web open URL PROFILE lx`) or as the default
 (`web config engine lx`): fast and small, no picture layer, a page as
 text and blocks.
 .
 It is WebKit, not Chrome: no Widevine, no Chrome extensions or sync. The
 Browser app and its settings come from the catalogue
 (`catalogue install apps/browser`), not from this package.
 .
 The module is built for hibr module ABI 17.

